    "https://explorejobs.uml.edu/en-us/job/530371/faculty-parttime-psychology": {
      "title": "Faculty Part-Time - Psychology",
      "description": "Faculty Part-Time - Psychology Apply now Job no: 530371 Position type: Faculty Part Time/Adjunct Benefit Status: Non-Benefited - Union Campus: UMass Lowell Department: Psychology Applications Open: Oct 08 2026 Applications Close: Open until filled General Summary of Position: The Psychology Department in the College of Fine Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences at the University of Massachusetts Lowell seeks applicants for an adjunct faculty position teaching a regularly offered, on-campus undergraduate course in Sport and Exercise Psychology . Candidates with expertise in additional areas of psychology represented in the department's curriculum may also be considered for other teaching opportunities, depending on departmental needs and course availability. Successful candidates will demonstrate expertise in the relevant subject area and a commitment to effective, engaging undergraduate teaching. The University of Massachusetts Lowell is committed to increasing diversity in its faculty, staff, and student populations. Minimum Qualifications (Required): Applicants must have an M.A. in Psychology, or closely related disciplines by the start of the appointment to be considered Ability to teach an undergraduate course in Sport and Exercise Psychology Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Psychology or closely related discipline Teaching experience in higher education Professional work experience with individual athletes and teams Prior experience with Canvas or other LMS systems Special Instructions to Applicants: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. However, the position may close when an adequate number of qualified applications is received. This is a part-time, non-benefited, Union of Adjunct Faculty, Local 1596, UAW position. For Adjunct Faculty salaries, please refer to the Adjunct Faculty salary chart for the rates. Please include a CV, cover letter, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (